# One build context for all three OSDU Delivery images: the repository root.
#
# The .NET images publish hosts under osdu/hosts, which reference both osdu/src and sqlflow/src (and central package
# management lives in osdu/Directory.Packages.props and sqlflow/Directory.Packages.props), and the GUI image compiles
# osdu/gui together with the vendored sqlflow/gui sources it imports. No image can be built from a narrower context.
#
# Never copy build output, git history or IDE state into a build: the publish and the npm build rebuild from source.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
.git/
.github/
**/*.user
artifacts/
TestResults/
**/.sqlflow/
**/node_modules/
**/*.md

# Generated GUI output and test artifacts. The e2e SOURCES stay in the context on purpose: osdu/gui/tsconfig.node.json
# compiles them as part of `tsc -b`, so excluding them would fail the GUI image's build.
**/gui/dist/
**/gui/.tsbuild/
**/gui/playwright-report/
**/gui/test-results/
**/gui/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/gui/e2e/.fixtures/

# Documentation: read by people, never by a build.
docs/
osdu/docs/
sqlflow/docs/

# Trees no image reads. Every root-context build tars the whole repository before the daemon applies these rules,
# so excluding them is what keeps a build submitting in seconds rather than minutes.
sqlflow/next-app/
sqlflow/_probe_sql/
sqlflow/data/
sqlflow/media/
sqlflow/logo/
sqlflow/schemas/
